# QA Agent Pro — configuration (.env)
# Read at server startup; restart your MCP client after editing.

# --- LLM credentials: NONE REQUIRED -------------------------------------
# This edition generates test cases in YOUR OWN chat model -- the editor
# you connected it to. The server calls no model at all: since
# 2026-08-16 llm.py has no backend and no API entry point, so there is
# no key and no CLI login to configure, and no setting that names one.
# qa-doctor reports nothing about a backend either -- there is none to
# probe, and telling you to fix one would describe a capability this
# product does not have.

# --- Features -----------------------------------------------------------
# Swagger/OpenAPI link -> API test cases. ALWAYS ON since 2026-08-13:
# the flag that used to carry it was deleted and the behaviour hardcoded
# to the `true` this edition always shipped, so there is nothing to set.
# Feature Analysis is not reachable on this edition and never was:
# since 2026-08-03 the test-cases-only build does not register
# qa_feature_analysis / qa_submit_feature_analysis at all. Their mobile
# modes described captured screens with this server's OWN vision call --
# the last tester-facing path that needed a credential. The flag that
# used to carry them was deleted on 2026-08-13; the edition gate is and
# always was the thing that decides it here.
# Device screens -> test cases, and learning from your past suites, are
# ALWAYS ON since 2026-08-13: QA_MOBILE_CAPTURE and QA_RAG_ENABLED were
# deleted and hardcoded to the `true` this edition always shipped, so
# there is nothing to set. qa_capture_screens stays LIVE -- it is how a
# tester grounds a Jira ticket's cases in the real screens, since Jira
# returns attachment metadata but never bytes -- and the screenshots ride
# to YOUR chat model as MCP image content: no server-side vision call, no
# API key. qa_search_corpus, the grounding block and the duplicate flags
# are always available; the QA_RAG_* knobs below are what you tune.
# 2026-08-01: bm25 -> cosine. BM25's IDF weighting COLLAPSES TOWARD ZERO
# for terms that come to dominate the corpus -- and any tester's corpus
# accumulates exactly that over time (repeated tickets, recurring
# features). Verified directly: on a 1524-entry corpus dominated by one
# repeated feature, the query with the MOST real matching history
# scored LOWEST (0.052) while an unrelated query scored HIGHEST (0.524)
# -- an INVERTED ranking, not a miscalibrated threshold. TF-IDF cosine
# does not have this pathology and ranked the same corpus correctly
# (0.702 for the real match vs 0.291 for the unrelated control).
QA_RAG_SIMILARITY_MODE=cosine
# Fresh suites rank slightly higher.
QA_RAG_RECENCY_HALF_LIFE_DAYS=30
# Corpus cap — oldest entries pruned beyond this.
QA_RAG_MAX_ENTRIES=5000
# Relevance floor for the 'Similar Past Test Cases' block injected into
# the prompt. Recalibrated for cosine's empirically observed range on a
# real corpus (~0.2-0.3 for an unrelated query, ~0.6-0.7 for a genuine
# topical match). The scale is MODE-dependent, so this value belongs
# with QA_RAG_SIMILARITY_MODE=cosine above; 0 disables it.
QA_RAG_SIMILAR_MIN_SCORE=0.4
# Duplicate-risk block's own threshold. The code default (0.3) was
# itself bm25-calibrated (see config/settings.py) and sits INSIDE
# cosine's observed 'unrelated' range (~0.29), which would false-flag
# unrelated cases as duplicates under cosine -- shipped explicitly
# above that range.
QA_RAG_SIMILARITY_THRESHOLD=0.55
# The startup re-registration pass was REMOVED on 2026-08-13 (flag
# deleted, hardcoded off): nothing writes to your editor configs
# unattended. Installed another editor since? Run
# ~/qa-agent-pro/connect.sh, which qa-doctor points you at.
# connect.sh / connect.ps1 and qa-doctor now ALWAYS offer to add the
# Atlassian (Jira Cloud) MCP entry for you instead of you hand-editing
# mcpServers JSON (the flag that governed it was deleted the same day and
# hardcoded to the ON it already shipped, so nothing changes for you).
# They only ADD a missing entry -- an existing `atlassian` entry is never
# touched -- and the write is atomic, locked and backed up. It does NOT
# log you in: OAuth is still one click in the editor. Claude Desktop is
# unaffected, because its Atlassian Connector lives in claude.ai settings
# and not in a file.
# Interactive pickers (Cursor 1.5+, Claude Code) are ALWAYS ON since
# 2026-08-13: QA_MCP_ELICIT_ENABLED was deleted and hardcoded to the
# `true` this edition always shipped. Clients without dialog support
# (Claude Desktop) still fall back to a text menu automatically.
# Folder for auto-exported .xlsx files, relative to the install dir.
# Files persist here across sessions and updates. Keep the comment on its
# OWN line: a value with a trailing comment reads fine to python-dotenv,
# but it has been echoed back verbatim when a host was asked where to save.
QA_EXPORT_DIR=data/exports
# Sub-task tickets: pull the parent story in as background context.
JIRA_FETCH_PARENT=true
# Cap on that background block, so a big epic cannot crowd out the sub-task.
JIRA_MAX_PARENT_CHARS=2500
# Sibling USER STORIES under the same parent, WITH their descriptions and
# acceptance criteria -- not just their titles. A sub-task carries a
# one-line summary while the requirements live in the parent AND in the
# stories beside it. Adds ONE search call to the fetch, and only when the
# ticket has a parent. The text goes into the clearly-labelled BACKGROUND
# block (never as the thing under test, every URL stripped).
JIRA_FETCH_SIBLING_STORIES=true
# Characters the sibling block may use, ADDITIVE to JIRA_MAX_PARENT_CHARS
# so sibling text can never truncate the parent's own description.
JIRA_MAX_SIBLING_CHARS=3000
# Searching the other Jira custom fields for one whose VALUE reads like
# requirements when JIRA_AC_FIELD does not was REMOVED on 2026-08-13
# (flag deleted, hardcoded off): adopting the wrong field is the failure
# it guarded against. Nothing that made that survivable changed -- a
# date-shaped value is still rejected, the description is still parsed,
# your own model is still asked to derive criteria, and qa-doctor still
# prints the configured field.
# Asking your own chat model to judge whether each generated case's
# expected result follows from the ticket was REMOVED the same day (flag
# deleted, hardcoded off): it changed what your model was asked to do and
# cost one judgement per case for an unmeasured precision.
# Ticket comments. Costs nothing extra: comments come back in the SAME
# getJiraIssue call your Atlassian MCP connection already makes. A ticket
# description is a snapshot taken at refinement, while the requirements
# that are actually current accumulate in the comment thread.
JIRA_FETCH_COMMENTS=true
JIRA_MAX_COMMENTS=5
# Image attachments. This does NOT give the model vision: your Atlassian
# MCP connection returns attachment metadata (name/type/size), never the
# image bytes. What you get is the filenames as context, plus a notice
# naming them and asking you to drag those screenshots into the chat --
# where they ARE read. Without it, a suite was generated from ticket text
# that never saw the screenshots and nothing said so.
JIRA_FETCH_IMAGES=true
# Server-side attachment DOWNLOAD was REMOVED on 2026-08-13 (flag
# deleted, hardcoded off): this server makes NO credentialed outbound
# request at all. Drag a ticket's screenshots into the chat and your own
# model reads them, exactly as it does today.
# HOST MODE: the parent chat fans out one same-session worker per
# category (Cursor Task / equivalent). Preferred finalize is Path B
# (merge then qa_submit_suite); Path A uses qa_submit_category +
# qa_prep_status. ALWAYS ON since 2026-08-13: the flag that carried it
# was deleted and hardcoded to the `true` this template already shipped,
# so there is nothing to set.

# How far back an ALREADY-FINISHED suite for the same ticket still earns
# a heads-up before another full generation starts. 24h by default,
# because this is an informational notice and not a refusal: the reply
# names the existing suite (id, case count, age), tells you how to
# re-export it, and `proceed_anyway=true` regenerates anyway. Observed
# 2026-08-10: one ticket generated three times in a day, seven stored
# suites, no warning. The separate IN-FLIGHT prep window
# (QA_HOST_DUPLICATE_PREP_WINDOW_S, 1800) is unchanged.
QA_HOST_DUPLICATE_SUITE_WINDOW_S=86400

# --- Updates & integrity ------------------------------------------------
# Releases are Ed25519-signed (MANIFEST.sig); verification is automatic.
# During migration an unsigned release still installs with a warning.
# Flip on once every live release is signed to REFUSE unsigned updates:
# QA_UPDATE_REQUIRE_SIGNATURE=1

# --- Jira -----------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing to set here. Paste a ticket URL and the agent reads it through
# your own Atlassian MCP connection (mcp.atlassian.com, OAuth) -- connect
# it once in your client's MCP settings. See docs/FEATURE_FLAGS.md.

# --- Usage analytics (telemetry) ---------------------------------------
# Anonymous usage metrics (tool name, version, OS, timings, success).
# ON by default; see the README 'Telemetry & privacy' section. Opt out
# with the cross-tool standard variable -- since 2026-08-13 this is the
# ONLY opt-out (QA_TELEMETRY_DISABLED was deleted):
# DO_NOT_TRACK=1
# Optionally identify this install (known teams only - sets person email):
# QA_USER_EMAIL=you@company.com
